# Optional. Copy to .env.development (used by `pnpm dev`) or .env.production
# (used by `pnpm build`). None of these are secrets. Without any of them the
# build serves https://app.weldsuite.eu and is pinned to the development
# extension id (src/manifest/dev-key.ts), which WeldID's weldsuite-extension
# client accepts. `pnpm zip` (the store build) ignores VITE_EXTENSION_KEY.

# Another default server, e.g. EU test. The manifest grants host access to
# exactly this server and its sign-in server.
# VITE_DEFAULT_SERVER=https://app.test.weldsuite.eu
# VITE_DEFAULT_ISSUER=https://auth.test.weldsuite.eu

# Another public key (base64) to pin the extension id, instead of the
# development key. Its id's redirect, https://<id>.chromiumapp.org/, must be
# on WeldID's weldsuite-extension client.
# VITE_EXTENSION_KEY=
